# TypeScript Standards

- Prefer explicit, domain-focused types for public function inputs/outputs.
- Avoid `any`; use `unknown` with narrowing when type is uncertain.
- Keep functions small and single-purpose; extract helpers instead of deep nesting.
- Handle async failures with meaningful errors; do not silently swallow exceptions with empty `catch`.
- Reuse existing Zod schemas before introducing new validation styles.
